{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And Elohim saw the children of Israel.</b> He attended to them and no longer hid His face from them, as in כִּי רָאִיתִי אֶת עַמִּי, כִּי בָאָה צַעֲקָתוֹ אֵלָי (1 Samuel 9:16) — just as He testified afterward, saying רָאֹה רָאִיתִי אֶת עֳנִי עַמִּי אֲשֶׁר בְּמִצְרָיִם (Exodus 3:7)." "<b>And Elohim knew.</b> He knew the afflictions of their heart, and that their prayer and cry was with a whole heart, as He recounted afterward, saying כִּי יָדַעְתִּי אֶת מַכְאֹבָיו (Exodus 3:7) — the opposite of וַיְפַתּוּהוּ בְּפִיהֶם וְלִבָּם לֹא נָכוֹן עִמּוֹ (Psalms 78:36-37)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:05.635310818Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}